This crate talks to Blackmagic Design DeckLink hardware through the Desktop
Video SDK (16.0). The SDK API headers and dispatch sources are redistributed
under the Blackmagic Source License in `decklink-sys/vendor/decklink` (see the
README there); every header keeps its original BSL notice. The runtime
libraries and drivers are NOT redistributed. You must install the Desktop Video
drivers from Blackmagic Design and accept their EULA:

  https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/EULA/DeckLinkSDK
  https://www.blackmagicdesign.com/desktopvideo_sdk

With `--features hardware` the build uses the vendored headers, so no separate
SDK download is needed on Windows, macOS or Linux. Set DECKLINK_SDK_DIR to
prefer headers from a full SDK install instead. On Windows the build also needs
the Visual Studio C++ toolchain and midl.exe so that DeckLinkAPI.idl can be
compiled. On Linux the installed libDeckLinkAPI.so is loaded at runtime. On
macOS the DeckLinkAPI.framework bundle is loaded at runtime.

